{
  "title": "Anticoagulants — High-Yield Notes (Board Review)",
  "background_color": "#EAF2F8",
  "citation": "Citations: DOI 10.1056/NEJMra2400000 | DOI 10.1161/AHA.120.017520 | Sources: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42209153/",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "core_concept",
      "title": "Core Concept",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 58,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 155,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#2980B9",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "path": "/home/ubuntu/skills/scientific-infographics/templates/icon_blood_vessel.png",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 34,
          "width": 230,
          "height": 108
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Anticoagulants inhibit fibrin formation (Inhibit Fibrin Formation).",
          "x": 252,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 13,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 298
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Prevent thrombosis by inhibiting coagulation cascade\n- Used mainly for DVT, PE, AF stroke prevention",
          "x": 252,
          "y": 72,
          "font_size": 12,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 298
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "major_classes",
      "title": "Major Classes",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 226,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 100,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#2980B9",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Vitamin K antagonists (Warfarin)",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 13,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Direct oral anticoagulants (DOACs)",
          "x": 285,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 13,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 265
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Heparins (UFH, LMWH)",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 58,
          "font_size": 13,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "   - Xa inhibitors: apixaban, rivaroxaban",
          "x": 285,
          "y": 58,
          "font_size": 12,
          "color": "#5D6D7E",
          "max_width": 265
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Indirect Xa inhibitor (Fondaparinux)",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 78,
          "font_size": 13,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "   - Thrombin inhibitor: dabigatran",
          "x": 285,
          "y": 78,
          "font_size": 12,
          "color": "#5D6D7E",
          "max_width": 265
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "warfarin",
      "title": "1. Warfarin (VKA)",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 338,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 315,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#1A5276",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "path": "/home/ubuntu/skills/scientific-infographics/templates/icon_liver.png",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 34,
          "width": 75,
          "height": 75
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "x": 92,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 175
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Inhibits VKOR → ↓ synthesis of Factors II, VII, IX, X + Protein C/S",
          "x": 92,
          "y": 54,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 175
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Key Points",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 118,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Delayed onset (days) → requires heparin bridge\n- Initial hypercoagulable state (↓ protein C first)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 136,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Monitoring",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 180,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- PT/INR (target ≈2–3)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 198,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reversal",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 218,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Vitamin K (slow)\n- PCC (fast) ± FFP",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 236,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Adverse Effects (HIGH-YIELD)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 268,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#C0392B",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Skin necrosis (early)\n- Teratogenic\n- Bleeding",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 286,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "heparins",
      "title": "2. Heparins",
      "x": 305,
      "y": 338,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 315,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#1A5276",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Activates Antithrombin III (ATIII) → inhibits Xa and IIa (Thrombin)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "UFH (Unfractionated Heparin)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 92,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- IV, rapid onset/offset\n- Monitor: aPTT\n- Reversal: protamine sulfate",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 110,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "LMWH (e.g., enoxaparin)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 162,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Mainly Xa inhibition\n- SC, predictable\n- Minimal monitoring\n- Renally cleared",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 180,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Adverse Effects (HIGH-YIELD)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 240,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#C0392B",
          "max_width": 255
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "HIT (VERY HIGH YIELD)\n- ↓ platelets + paradoxical thrombosis\n- Osteoporosis (long-term)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 258,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 255
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fondaparinux",
      "title": "3. Fondaparinux",
      "x": 600,
      "y": 58,
      "width": 285,
      "height": 190,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#1E8449",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 265
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Fondaparinux → ATIII → inhibits Xa",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 265
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Key Features",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 90,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 265
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Indirect Xa inhibitor (via antithrombin)\n- No HIT risk\n- Minimal monitoring (anti-Xa if needed)\n- Renally cleared\n- No specific reversal agent",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 108,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 265
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "doacs",
      "title": "4. Direct Oral Anticoagulants (DOACs)",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 58,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 295,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#6C3483",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Classes",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Xa Inhibitors: apixaban, rivaroxaban (-xaban)\n- Thrombin inhibitor: dabigatran",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Advantages",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 90,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Oral, rapid onset\n- No routine monitoring\n- Fewer interactions",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 108,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Limitations",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 150,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#C0392B",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Renal dosing\n- Not for: Mechanical valves\n- Antiphospholipid syndrome",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 168,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reversal (VERY TESTABLE)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 210,
          "font_size": 12,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A252F",
          "max_width": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Dabigatran → idarucizumab\n- Xa inhibitors → andexanet alfa\n- PCC if unavailable",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 228,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#2C3E50",
          "max_width": 260
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "key_comparisons",
      "title": "Key Comparisons",
      "x": 600,
      "y": 260,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 135,
      "background_color": "#FDFEFE",
      "header_color": "#2980B9",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 34,
          "headers": ["Drug", "Monitoring", "Reversal", "Pregnancy"],
          "rows": [
            ["Warfarin", "INR", "Vit K + PCC", "X"],
            ["UFH", "aPTT", "Protamine", "OK"],
            ["LMWH", "Minimal", "Partial protamine", "OK"],
            ["DOACs", "None", "Specific agents", "X"]
          ],
          "col_widths": [95, 105, 200, 95],
          "row_height": 22,
          "header_bg": "#D6EAF8",
          "alt_row_bg": "#EBF5FB"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exam_pearls",
      "title": "Exam Pearls",
      "x": 600,
      "y": 406,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 120,
      "background_color": "#EBF5FB",
      "header_color": "#117A65",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Warfarin → bridge with heparin",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 280
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Protamine reverses heparin",
          "x": 298,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 275
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "HIT = thrombosis + thrombocytopenia",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 280
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Idarucizumab = dabigatran antidote",
          "x": 298,
          "y": 54,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 275
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "DOACs = no monitoring",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 72,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 280
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Andexanet = Xa inhibitor antidote",
          "x": 298,
          "y": 72,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 275
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Protamine reverses heparin",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 90,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 280
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Heparin safe in pregnancy",
          "x": 298,
          "y": 90,
          "font_size": 11,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 275
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "one_liner",
      "title": "One-Liner",
      "x": 600,
      "y": 537,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 100,
      "background_color": "#EBF5FB",
      "header_color": "#117A65",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"Anticoagulants inhibit fibrin formation — warfarin affects synthesis, heparin enhances antithrombin, DOACs directly block Xa or thrombin.\"",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 36,
          "font_size": 13,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "#1A5276",
          "max_width": 562
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
